# Loop MIDI storage, validation, and undo

Before changing loop event storage, capture/commit, stop-path validation, undo, or SD loop I/O, read:

**[`docs/Guides/LOOP_MIDI_STORAGE_AND_VALIDATION.md`](docs/Guides/LOOP_MIDI_STORAGE_AND_VALIDATION.md)**

Related guides: [`NOTE_WRAPPING_LOGIC.md`](docs/Guides/NOTE_WRAPPING_LOGIC.md) (display only), plans [`overdub_undo_baseline_phase1_refinement.md`](docs/plans/overdub_undo_baseline_phase1_refinement.md) and [`memory_scalability_refactor_enhancement.md`](docs/plans/memory_scalability_refactor_enhancement.md).

## Non-negotiable constraints

- **Playback / hot paths:** `loop.eventAt()` / `committedEvents.readStore()` — not full flatten.
- **Stop path:** `finalizeLoopAtStop` + `LoopStopFinalize` (wrap window only). Do **not** call full `validateAndCleanupMidiEvents` on record/overdub stop.
- **Full validate:** deferred via `processDeferredIdleMaintenance` when transport idle, or on SD load — not on stop.
- **Undo snapshots:** always `cloneShared()` / `restoreFromSnapshot` — never shallow-copy chunk IDs.
- **Undo routing:** overdub undo before clear-slot undo in `handleUndo`; `clearClearUndoStacks()` on `startRecording`.
- **Overdub entry:** `beginOverdubSession` only — no extra `pushUndoSnapshot` at overdub start (Phase 1).
- **After flat edits:** `invalidateCaches()` so chunks and note cache stay in sync.
- **SD:** flatten on save/load; chunk IDs are in-RAM only until a format version bump.
- **Hot path:** no `MemoryMonitor` walks or full-loop sort on record/overdub stop.

## Primary files

`LoopEventStore.*`, `LoopEventBuffer.h`, `Loop.h`, `Loop.cpp`, `Track.cpp`, `TrackUndo.cpp`, `Utils/LoopStopFinalize.h`, `StorageManager.cpp`, `main.cpp` (idle maintenance).

## Tests

After logic changes: `pio test -e native` (`test_loop_event_store`, `test_loop_stop_finalize`, `test_noteutils_reconstruct`).
